# Output Contract

End every **implementation** task (code, config, migrations, CI/CD) with this structure. Omit sections that do not apply only when the task was purely Q&A with no changes — otherwise keep the full shape and be brief.

Omit unnecessary explanations unrelated to the task.

## Summary

- What changed (and why, in one line if useful)

## Files Changed

- Each changed file and purpose

## Validation

- Commands run and results; if not run, why and what was verified manually

## Quality Review

- Code quality, typing, security, performance, deployment considerations (relevant gates only)

## Risks / Notes

- Assumptions, risks, compatibility, follow-ups; note Ponytail trade-offs if a deliberate simplification was used

## Final checklist

- Change addresses the request
- Existing conventions preserved; incremental and low-risk
- Frontend/backend contracts consistent when both touched
- Error handling explicit; security/performance/deployment reviewed as relevant
- Tests/validation run or documented
- No unrelated files modified; no secrets exposed

Incomplete checklist items must be explained.
